From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:55:44 +0200
Subject: soc: sunxi: mbus: drop the A80 display engine

The A80 display backend reads DRAM with CPU physical addresses. With the
MBUS offset applied, it fetches the framebuffer from below DRAM, and
HDMI shows a white screen.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_mbus.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_mbus.c b/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_mbus.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_mbus.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_mbus.c
@@ -23,7 +23,6 @@ static const char * const sunxi_mbus_devices[] = {
 	"allwinner,sun7i-a20-display-engine",
 	"allwinner,sun8i-a23-display-engine",
 	"allwinner,sun8i-a33-display-engine",
-	"allwinner,sun9i-a80-display-engine",
 
 	/*
 	 * And now we have the regular devices connected to the MBUS
@@ -50,7 +49,6 @@ static const char * const sunxi_mbus_devices[] = {
 	"allwinner,sun8i-h3-csi",
 	"allwinner,sun8i-h3-video-engine",
 	"allwinner,sun8i-v3s-csi",
-	"allwinner,sun9i-a80-display-backend",
 	"allwinner,sun50i-a64-csi",
 	"allwinner,sun50i-a64-video-engine",
 	"allwinner,sun50i-h5-video-engine",
-- 
